<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Giambattista Bodoni</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1740–1813</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Giambattista Bodoni was an Italian printer and type designer from Saluzzo who directed the ducal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/printing-press">printing</a> house in Parma from 1768. His elegant typefaces, with strong contrast between thick and thin strokes, defined the modern or Didone style, and his Manuale tipografico was published after his death in 1818. Typefaces named after him are still widely used.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/giambattista-bodoni.jpg" alt="Giambattista Bodoni" width="320" height="410" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Giuseppe Lucatelli (1751-1828) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Giambattista_Bodoni_by_Giuseppe_Lucatelli.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
